# Phishing URL Classification using Snowflake ML

## 📌 Project Overview

Phishing URL Classification is a machine learning classification project developed using **Python, Scikit-learn, Snowflake and Streamlit**.

The system analyzes characteristics extracted from a URL and predicts whether the URL is likely to be a **legitimate URL or a phishing URL**.

The trained machine learning model is deployed as an interactive Streamlit application in Snowflake.

## 🎯 Objective

The main objective of this project is to develop a machine learning model that can classify URLs based on extracted URL characteristics and provide a prediction through an interactive web application.

## 📊 Dataset

**Dataset:** Phishing URL Dataset with Extracted Features

**Source:** Kaggle

**Dataset Link:**
https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/victusadi/phishing-urls-dataset-with-extracted-features

The dataset contains URLs along with extracted features used for phishing URL classification.

## 🔍 Features Used

The machine learning pipeline uses the following 11 input features:

* URL_LENGTH
* NUM_DOTS
* HAS_HTTPS
* HAS_IP
* NUM_SUBDIRS
* NUM_PARAMS
* SUSPICIOUS_WORDS
* TLD
* SPECIAL_CHAR_COUNT
* DIGITS_COUNT
* ENTROPY

## 🤖 Machine Learning Model

### Random Forest Classifier

A **Random Forest Classifier** was trained for the phishing URL classification task.

The saved model includes the complete preprocessing and classification pipeline.

The preprocessing pipeline includes:

* Missing-value imputation
* StandardScaler for numerical features
* One-hot encoding for the TLD feature
* Random Forest classification



